# Settings of the self-hosted Free Planning Poker (deploy/compose.yml). Copy this file to `.env` beside the compose file and
# fill in the two secrets; the commands on https://free-planning-poker.com/self-hosting do both. `.env` holds secrets: keep it
# out of version control.
#
# A value is read when the containers start: after a change run `docker compose up -d --wait`.

# ---- Secrets: no default, the start stops with a message that names the one that is missing ----

# The password of the database user. It sits inside a URL, so use letters and digits only: openssl rand -hex 24
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# The key behind the visitor hash (the counts of visitors per day): at least 32 characters, never shared, never changed
# after the first start unless you accept that the next day's visitors are all counted as new. openssl rand -hex 32
VISITOR_KEY=

# ---- Where the room is served ----

# The origins a browser opens the room from, comma-separated, exactly as the address bar shows them
# (scheme://host[:port], no path). Default: http://localhost:<FPP_PORT> and http://127.0.0.1:<FPP_PORT>, which is right
# for this machine. Behind your own domain set it to that origin, e.g. https://poker.example.com. A browser whose origin is
# not listed is refused the room socket, and so is the contact and feedback form.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://poker.example.com

# The port on the host. Default: 7740.
# FPP_PORT=7740

# The address the port is published on. Default: 127.0.0.1, this machine only, for a reverse proxy on the same host. Set
# 0.0.0.0 to publish it on every interface. The image speaks plain HTTP: TLS is a proxy's job and is not part of this file.
# FPP_BIND=127.0.0.1

# The request header your proxy sets to the client's address, e.g. cf-connecting-ip behind Cloudflare. It must be a header
# the proxy overwrites, never x-forwarded-for. Unset: the limit on wrong access codes counts the address of the connection,
# which behind a proxy is the proxy.
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER=

# ---- The image ----

# The image to run. Default: ghcr.io/jkrumm/free-planning-poker:latest, the newest build of master. Pin a release or a commit
# for updates you decide on, e.g. ghcr.io/jkrumm/free-planning-poker:9.0.0 or ghcr.io/jkrumm/free-planning-poker:sha-1a2b3c4.
# FPP_IMAGE=ghcr.io/jkrumm/free-planning-poker:latest

# ---- Optional services: all off while unset ----

# Telemetry: the base URL of an OpenTelemetry collector (OTLP over HTTP). Unset: nothing is built and nothing is exported.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=

# The contact form (POST /api/contact) sends through a mail gateway: its base URL and its secret, both or neither. Unset: the
# form answers 503 "unavailable" and nothing is sent.
# EMAIL_GATEWAY_URL=
# EMAIL_GATEWAY_SECRET_KEY=

# The feedback route (POST /api/feedback) hands feedback to an issue tracker's HTTP door: its full URL and a token, both or
# neither. Unset: the route answers 503 "unavailable".
# FACTORY_FEEDBACK_URL=
# FACTORY_FEEDBACK_TOKEN=

# Web analytics (Umami) is not a setting of this image: it sends nothing to an analytics host, and none runs beside it.
